#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:5
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:8
msgid "On this page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:11
msgid "Install or update the add-on on an already-existing Odoo installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:13
msgid "There are multiple options to install this add-on"
msgstr "Il existe plusieurs options pour installer cet add-on"

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:15
msgid "Install from the Odoo Apps store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:17
msgid ""
"Navigate to `the module’s apps.odoo.com page "
"<https://apps.odoo.com/apps/modules/18.0/payment_taler>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:19
msgid "Click on ``Deploy on Odoo.sh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:20
msgid "The add-on should be now installed on your Odoo.sh instance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:22
msgid "Manually add the code yourself in your Odoo install (Multiple options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:25
msgid "First, download the add-on code with either of these 3 methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:27
msgid ""
"Download the latest version from the releases "
"(https://codeberg.org/Nemael/tops/releases)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:30
msgid "Downloading the latest release provides the most stable and tested code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:33
msgid ""
"Download the add-on from `the apps.odoo.com page "
"<https://apps.odoo.com/apps/modules/18.0/payment_taler>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:35
msgid "Clone this repository (git clone https://codeberg.org/Nemael/tops.git)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:38
msgid "Preferably clone it in ``{your Odoo install}/custom_addons``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:40
msgid "Ensure that the ``tops`` directory is in ``custom_addons``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:41
msgid ""
"Cloning the repository provides the most up-to-date code, and you can "
"simply use ``git pull`` to obtain the latest updates. However, the code "
"obtained this way might be unstable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:46
msgid "Then move the files to your Odoo folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:48
msgid "Extract the zip file to ``{your Odoo install}/custom_addons``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:49
msgid ""
"Ensure that the ``tops`` or ``payment_taler`` directory is in "
"``custom_addons``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:53
msgid ""
"Note: the add-on code can be stored anywhere, but it’s easier store it "
"within the Odoo folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:55
msgid ""
"In the command line you used to start Odoo, specify the path to this add-"
"on by adding the argument ``--addons-path=./addons,./custom_addons/tops``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:59
msgid ""
"Such as: ``./odoo-bin --addons-path=./addons,./custom_addons/tops -u tops"
" -d odoo18_tops_0.1.1.1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:62
msgid "In Odoo, go to the ``Apps`` section in the app switcher (top-left button)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:64
msgid "Click ``Update Apps List`` on the top bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:65
msgid "Search for the add-on ``Taler-Odoo Payment System``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:66
msgid ""
"Click on the add-on, and press ``Activate`` or ``Install`` to complete "
"this step"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:71
msgid ""
"To update the add-on, first update the code using the same way that you "
"first downloaded it, then restart the server and finally click "
"``Upgrade`` on the add-on page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:77
msgid "Uninstall the add-on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:79
msgid "To uninstall the add-on, you have to go to the ``Apps`` app on Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:80
msgid "Search for, and go to the ``Taler-Odoo Payment System`` add-on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:81
msgid "Click ``Uninstall``, the add-on should be uninstalled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:84
msgid ""
"If you have made any transactions using Taler with this add-on, you will "
"not be able to uninstall it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:86
msgid "You can reinstall the add-on at a later time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:87
msgid ""
"If you added a payment method record for the point of sale app (:ref:`see"
" the related section for more information <point-of-sale-payment-"
"configuration>`), complete the following steps as well:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:89
msgid ""
"Go to the ``Point of Sale`` app, and navigate to ``Configuration/Payment "
"Methods``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:91
msgid ""
"Click on the ``Taler`` record you created when setting up the point of "
"sale payment system, it should be highlighted in red because the payment "
"provider is not available anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:94
msgid ""
"Click on the gear at the top, and then either ``Archive`` (better for "
"data conservation) or ``Delete`` (more risky because you might lose track"
" of some payments)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:97
msgid "On the top bar, go to ``Configuration -> Point of Sales``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:98
msgid "Select a point of sale that you made Taler payments available for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:99
msgid ""
"Click on ``More settings: Configurations > Settings``, which will lead "
"you to the point of sale’s settings page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:101
msgid "In Payment -> Payment Methods, remove the Taler payment method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user-guide/installation.rst:103
msgid ""
"Do this step for every point of sale you made Taler payments available "
"for."
msgstr ""

